# Recovering Access to a Former Employee's OneDrive Using SharePoint Online PowerShell

## Overview

This project demonstrates how to recover administrative access to a former employee's OneDrive site after the account has been disabled or the employee has departed the organization.

Using SharePoint Online PowerShell, the administrator:

- Connected to the SharePoint Online Admin Center
- Verified the OneDrive site status
- Removed the ReadOnly lock
- Assigned a Site Collection Administrator
- Restored access for data retrieval and business continuity

---

## Environment

| Component | Details |
|------------|-----------|
| Platform | Microsoft 365 |
| Service | SharePoint Online |
| Storage | OneDrive for Business |
| Tool | SharePoint Online Management Shell |
| Access Level | SharePoint Administrator |

---

## Business Scenario

A former employee's OneDrive contained company files that needed to be reviewed and transferred to management.

The OneDrive site was in a **ReadOnly** state, preventing modifications and administrative access.

Using SharePoint Online PowerShell, administrative ownership was granted to an authorized employee so the files could be reviewed, archived, or migrated as required.

---

## Step 1: Connect to SharePoint Online

```powershell
Connect-SPOService -Url "https://tenant-admin.sharepoint.com"
```

---

## Step 2: Verify OneDrive Site Status

```powershell
Get-SPOSite -Identity "https://tenant-my.sharepoint.com/personal/user_company_com" |
Select Url, LockState, Status
```

### Initial Output

```text
Url                                                                   LockState Status
---                                                                   --------- ------
https://"insert_user_company".sharepoint.com/personal/...            ReadOnly  Active
```

The site was active but locked in a ReadOnly state.

---

## Step 3: Unlock the OneDrive Site

```powershell
Set-SPOSite `
-Identity "https://tenant-my.sharepoint.com/personal/user_company_com" `
-LockState Unlock
```

---

## Step 4: Verify the Site is Unlocked

```powershell
Get-SPOSite `
-Identity "https://"insert_user_company".sharepoint.com/personal/insert_user_email" |
Select Url, LockState, Status
```

### Verification Output

```text
Url                                                                   LockState Status
---                                                                   --------- ------
https://"insert_user_company".sharepoint.com/personal/...            Unlock    Active
```

The OneDrive site was successfully unlocked.

---

## Step 5: Assign Site Collection Administrator

```powershell
Set-SPOUser `
-Site "https://tenant-my.sharepoint.com/personal/user_company_com" `
-LoginName "admin@company.com" `
-IsSiteCollectionAdmin $true
```

### Result

```text
Display Name      Login Name                          User Type
------------      ----------                          ---------
Rxxxxxx Cxxxxxx  insert_user_email                    Member
```

Administrative permissions were successfully assigned to the designated user.

---

